            <ArticleTitle>Early recognition of spinal cord compression in cancer patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>629-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spinal cord compression is a relatively common complication of a number of malignant diseases. Back pain is the presenting symptom in more than 90% of cases. Early recognition and prompt treatment, while the patient can still walk, are the most important factors in preventing permanent and debilitating neurologic dysfunction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
